From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nowon <nowon@noreply.pepecoin.surf>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 18:23:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 132/144] GreatDANE: restore official Sync promo and bookmarks;
 gate Dane IDs; drop Customize (round 4h)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

NGD 4f+4g LOW-MED / LOW: 0097 and 0098 leaked Dane wording and URLs into
official builds through shared sync.inc.xhtml, preferences.ftl, and
default-bookmarks.html. Same principle as NGD L1.

Official branding again uses the stock strings and URLs:
- sync-mobile-promo in en-US preferences.ftl is "Download Firefox for
  Android or iOS..."
- sync.inc.xhtml official branch has the stock Android/iOS icons and links
- default-bookmarks.html official branch has the stock Firefox/Mozilla
  artwork, help/customize/contribute URLs, and the NIGHTLY_BUILD block
- default-bookmarks.ftl stock titles are restored (Mozilla Firefox,
  Customize Firefox, Firefox Nightly Resources, ...)

Unofficial builds use new Dane-only Fluent IDs in greatdane brand.ftl,
which locales/jar.mn already ships to every locale, so a non-en-US Sync
promo no longer says "Téléchargez Firefox...":
- dane-sync-mobile-promo (desktop download page; Dane has no mobile app)
- dane-default-bookmarks-heading / get-help / community / about

Sync functionality and behaviour are unchanged. There is no hide of the
promo and no change to sync.js; only the unofficial promo wording/link is
gated. identity.mobilepromo.* in greatdane firefox-branding.js is unchanged.

Get involved (About dane-helpus and the unofficial Get Involved bookmark)
now points at https://dane.surf/source/ (public HTTPS 200, title "Dane
source code"). The unofficial About Support label stays in place of Terms.

Customize Dane is dropped on unofficial builds only: curl of
https://dane.surf/support/ (2026-11-10, America/Chicago) shows no heading
anchors (no id or name attributes to target). Official Customize Firefox
is unchanged.

Prepared only. Not built, signed, notarized or published.
